{"type":"failure","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-12T07:26:28.184Z","evidence":{"commit":"092239d660f14bc5035bca220a13aadf1fa804b9"},"description":"On Windows, a Python script that writes repository files with open(path, 'w') writes CRLF line endings, so LF files turn CRLF and git warns.","resolution":"Read and write with open(path, encoding='utf-8', newline=''). If it happened, run sed -i 's/\\r$//' on the file. Write scripts to a file outside the repository instead of a bash heredoc.","id":"mx-7d118a","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-13T22:34:03.572Z","archive_reason":"manual: duplicate: mx-51980d now holds all three CRLF lessons"}
